Subject: [PATCH] cuda_blackboard: replace cudaStreamGetDevice with cudaGetDevice

cudaStreamGetDevice doesn't just need the CUDA 12.8 headers to compile — it also needs the 12.8 driver at runtime.
JetPack 6.x tops out at the CUDA 12.6 driver, so the call returns
cudaErrorCallRequiresNewerDriver (36), which makes the pointcloud_container constructor throw
and abort — the entire point cloud preprocessing/concatenation chain disappears, and downstream this shows up as
  ndt_scan_matcher: No InputSource
  /api/localization/initialize: align server failed
which is highly misleading.

stream_ was created on the current device just two lines above, so reading the current device number via cudaGetDevice is equivalent,
and it carries no driver version requirement.

Tested on hardware (Orin AGX / JetPack 6.2 / L4T R36.4.3): before the patch, exactly 1 process died every run;
after the patch, 0 process deaths and 0 cudaErrors.
---
--- a/src/cuda_mem_pool_context.cpp
+++ b/src/cuda_mem_pool_context.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
   CUDA_BLACKBOARD_CHECK_CUDA_ERROR(cudaStreamCreateWithFlags(&free_stream_, cudaStreamNonBlocking));
 
   int device_id = 0;
-  CUDA_BLACKBOARD_CHECK_CUDA_ERROR(cudaStreamGetDevice(stream_, &device_id));
+  CUDA_BLACKBOARD_CHECK_CUDA_ERROR(cudaGetDevice(&device_id));
 
   cudaMemPoolProps pool_props = {};
   pool_props.allocType = cudaMemAllocationTypePinned;
